{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And it produced a blossom.</b> A sign for the blossoms of priesthood that would emerge from him." "<b>And it produced a bud.</b> A sign that priests would emerge from him who are zealous in their service, as we say: the priests are zealous — חז״ק. This is what we say in tractate Avot: also the staff of Aharon — its almond-blossom and its flower (cf. ״שקדיה ופרחיה״), which is among the things created at twilight on the eve of Shabbat."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The Aramaic phrase ואף מטהו של אהרן שקדיה ופרחיה is rendered literally; the reference is to Mishnah Avot 5:6, listing Aharon's staff among the ten things created bein ha-shemashot."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:26.210206769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}